For purposes of this Additional Use Grant:

"Competitive Offering" means a Product that is offered to third parties on a
paid basis, including through paid support arrangements, and that is
substantially similar to, or a commercial substitute for, HyperLyte's paid
version or paid versions of the Licensed Work. If your Product is not a
Competitive Offering when you first make it generally available, it will not
become a Competitive Offering later solely because HyperLyte releases a new
version of the Licensed Work with additional capabilities. Products that are
not provided on a paid basis are not Competitive Offerings.

"Product" means software, a hosted service, or an embedded service whose
primary functionality includes orchestration of artificial intelligence agents,
agent-assisted software development, agent-assisted code analysis, model
training, model testing, model development, or functionality that substantially
overlaps with the paid version or paid versions of the Licensed Work.

"Hosted" means running the Licensed Work, or a modified version or derivative
work of it, so that third parties can access the Licensed Work or any material
portion of its functionality over a network, API, command-line bridge, web UI,
IDE integration, extension, or other remote or managed interface.

"Embedded" means including source code or executable code from the Licensed
Work in a Competitive Offering. "Embedded" also means packaging a Competitive
Offering in such a way that the Licensed Work must be accessed or downloaded
for the Competitive Offering to operate.

Hosting or using the Licensed Work for internal purposes within an organization
is not a Competitive Offering. For this purpose, your organization includes all
affiliates under common control.

